    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616-a3">

                <pb facs="0724" n="628" xml:id="pg628"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mataafa to the Commission.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Malie</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: We received your excellencies’ letter
                    stating Monday, the 29th instant, to be the day on which you would come to
                    Malie. I comply with this entirely; so do all our chiefs.</p>
                <p>But we ask, with respect, that if it meets your wishes, Wednesday, the 31st
                    instant, may be appointed, so that I may be able to bring the guns which are at
                    Savaii, and deliver them together to you. Asking pardon for this,</p>
                <p>We remain, yours, truly,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mataafa and</hi> 13 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Chiefs of Tanua and Pule.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
